---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InPageNav from '../components/InPageNav.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Studio" description="Dead Signal Works is a solo studio building Project Meridian, the Meridian engine, and Alchemist." currentPath="/studio/">
  <section class="studio-page-hero">
    <div class="shell studio-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker"><span>Dead Signal Works LLC</span> / solo studio</p>
        <h1>A little about me and the mission.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="page-lede">Dead Signal Works is one person making games, software, and the technology that holds them together.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <InPageNav items={[
    { label: 'About', href: '#about' },
    { label: 'The mission', href: '#mission' },
    { label: 'The work', href: '#work' },
  ]} />

  <section class="content-section shell prose-split" id="about">
    <div><p class="section-number">01 / About</p><h2>One workbench, a lot of jobs.</h2></div>
    <div class="copy-stack">
      <p class="large-copy">I handle the game, engine, tools, design, direction, production, website, and the email you send through it.</p>
      <p>The studio is deliberately small. It gives the game and its technology room to grow together instead of being negotiated between separate companies.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="studio-mission" id="mission">
    <div class="shell studio-mission-grid">
      <p class="section-number">02 / The mission</p>
      <blockquote>Make realistic, highly performant games without treating the technology underneath them as somebody else’s fixed limit.</blockquote>
      <p>Dead Signal Works makes games that push the bounds of what is possible in a game engine. Meridian is how I make that practical.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section studio-work-board" id="work">
    <div class="shell studio-current-work">
      <div><p class="section-number">03 / The work</p><h2>Three projects, one workbench.</h2><p>Project Meridian is the game. Meridian is the engine being built alongside it. Alchemist is open-source media transcoding software with its own public release line.</p></div>
      <div class="work-pair">
        <a href="/project-meridian/"><span>Game</span><h3>Project Meridian</h3><p>Exploration-focused liminal horror.</p><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></a>
        <a href="/meridian/"><span>Engine</span><h3>Meridian</h3><p>Rust game technology relicensed to MPL-2.0 for open-source release.</p><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></a>
        <a href="/alchemist/"><span>Software</span><h3>Alchemist</h3><p>Self-hosted transcoding automation under AGPL-3.0-or-later.</p><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
